course: dictionary
lesson: 11828
title: Blab: when a secret slips out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To blab is an informal verb, so you will mostly meet it in chatty talk and stories. It means to tell a secret, often by talking carelessly without thinking about who is listening. «Mia promised not to blab about the surprise party, but she told Sam everything at lunch.» The clues are promised and told everything: Mia did not keep the secret.
explain: Blab has a second meaning: to talk too much about silly things. «Ben blabbed on and on about his new trainers, and nobody could get a word in.» The clue is on and on: he talked far too much. Someone who blabs is sometimes called a blabbermouth, which is also informal.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try "tell a secret" or "talk too much" instead of blab. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Blab is a verb: blab, blabs, blabbed, blabbing.
fact: «Blab» means to tell a secret, often by talking carelessly.
fact: «Blab» can also mean to talk too much about silly things.
fact: A «blabbermouth» is someone who blabs. It is an informal word.
fact: Useful phrases are «blab to», «blab about» and «don't blab».
exercise: «Please don't blab about the surprise party to Ellie.» What does blab mean here? | *To tell a secret carelessly | To count the guests | To hide the present | To sing a happy song
exercise: «Grandad blabbed on for an hour about the weather and his old car.» What does blabbed suggest? | He told a secret about a treasure | He fell asleep at the table | He whispered very quietly | *He talked too much about silly things
exercise: Which word is the name for someone who blabs? | blanket | *blabbermouth | bluebell | blossom
test: «Sam promised to keep the plan secret, but he blabbed it to the whole class.» What does blabbed mean here? | Wrote a poem | Shouted for help | *Told a secret carelessly | Ran very fast
test: Mum says, «Don't blab to your sister about her birthday present.» What should you not do? | Thank Grandad for the card | Wrap the present neatly | *Tell her the secret | Look at the present
exam: «Lily kept her secret safe and never blabbed, even when her friends begged her.» What does this tell you about Lily? | *She keeps secrets well | She loves birthday parties | She talks far too much | She cannot keep a secret
